{
  "schema_version": "1.6.2",
  "id": "BIT-gitea-2026-89430",
  "summary": "Gitea push mirror SSRF and forced writes to internal Git hosts",
  "details": "Gitea validated a push mirror's remote address against the `[migrations]` allow and block lists only when the mirror was created. Each synchronization passed the stored address directly to `git push`, so a name that later resolved to a blocked or internal address was still reached. A user with administrator access to a repository, which includes repositories they create themselves, could aim push mirror synchronization at internal Git services and force-push the repository's contents to them.",
